\section{Mathematical Foundations}

\subsection{Governing Equations}
AFDL-v1.0 evolves fluid states using a hybrid formulation combining
Navier--Stokes dynamics, Vlasov--Poisson phase-space evolution, and Hamiltonian
flow operators.

We define the core evolution operator:
\begin{equation}
  \mathcal{L}_{\text{AFDL}} =
  \mathcal{H}_{\text{flow}} +
  \mathcal{A}_{\text{AMR}} +
  \mathcal{S}_{\text{stability}},
\end{equation}
where:
\begin{itemize}
  \item $\mathcal{H}_{\text{flow}}$ is the Hamiltonian flow update operator.
  \item $\mathcal{A}_{\text{AMR}}$ is the autonomous mesh refinement operator.
  \item $\mathcal{S}_{\text{stability}}$ is the predictive stability operator.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Liouville Preservation}
AFDL-v1.0 enforces phase-space volume invariance under autonomous updates:
\begin{equation}
  \frac{d}{dt}\bigl(\text{Vol}_{\text{phase}}\bigr) = 0,
\end{equation}
ensuring Liouville preservation for the underlying Hamiltonian dynamics.

\subsection{Kolmogorov Complexity Bounds}
To prevent runaway refinement and uncontrolled solver branching, AFDL-v1.0
imposes a Kolmogorov complexity bound:
\begin{equation}
  K(\text{state}{t+1}) - K(\text{state}{t}) < \Delta K_{\max},
\end{equation}
where $K(\cdot)$ denotes Kolmogorov complexity and $\Delta K_{\max}$ is a
designer-chosen threshold.

\subsection{Non-Equilibrium Fluctuation Thresholds}
Autonomous mesh refinement is triggered when non-equilibrium fluctuations exceed
a critical threshold:
\begin{equation}
  \left\lvert \nabla S(x,t) \right\rvert > S_{\text{crit}},
\end{equation}
where $S(x,t)$ is an entropy-like stability metric and $S_{\text{crit}}$ is a
tunable parameter.

\section{Autonomous Loop Architecture}

\subsection{Predictive Stability Layer}
The predictive stability layer analyzes phase-space gradients and local
curvature of flow fields to anticipate instability before it manifests. This
layer feeds into the AMR controller and solver kernel to adjust resolution and
time-stepping.

\subsection{AMR Controller}
The AMR controller autonomously adjusts mesh resolution using:
\begin{itemize}
  \item Entropy gradients $\nabla S(x,t)$.
  \item Fluctuation metrics derived from local flow statistics.
  \item Curvature and shear indicators in the velocity and pressure fields.
\end{itemize}
Refinement and coarsening decisions are logged in the metadata spine.

\subsection{Solver Kernel}
The solver kernel executes fluid-dynamics updates using:
\begin{itemize}
  \item Measure-preserving numerical operators.
  \item High-order finite-volume or finite-difference schemes.
  \item Phase-space consistency checks to maintain Liouville invariance.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Metadata Spine}
At each timestep, the metadata spine records:
\begin{itemize}
  \item AMR decisions and refinement patterns.
  \item Stability triggers and threshold crossings.
  \item Solver tolerances and numerical parameters.
  \item Configuration signatures and hashes.
  \item Designer attribution hash linked to C.\ Matthew Blackwell.
\end{itemize}

